    "title": "Bulls vs. Thunder: Live updates, highlights for Friday's game",
    "text": "Updated March 27, 2026, 8:56 p.m. CTThe Oklahoma City Thunder will host the Chicago Bulls on Friday. This will be the second matchup of the season between the two squads. Last time, OKC pulled away late in a short-handed win on Mar. 3.The Thunder (57-16) couldn't come up with big-time moments in a 119-109 loss to the Boston Celtics on Wednesday. Shai Gilgeous-Alexander had 33 points and eight assists. It snapped their 12-game win streak.Meanwhile, the Bulls (29-43) continue to bottom out. They had a high-scoring 157-137 loss to the Philadelphia 76ers on Wednesday. Josh Giddey had 23 points, 12 assists and nine rebounds.For live updates of the Thunder's game against the Bulls, please regularly check back to this post: End 3Q: Thunder 95, Bulls 88Great response by the Thunder. After going 0-of-10 from 3, Gilgeous-Alexander has abandoned his outside jumper. That's helped him reach 25 points. The Bulls cooled off from the outside, relatively speaking. OKC had an 15-0 run to retake the lead and build some momentum. Let's see if they can close things out. Half: Bulls 67, Thunder 62Just an awful half by the Thunder. On defense, specifically. Letting the Bulls flirt with 70 points on your league-best defense just can't happen. Especially when it's by Okoro and Miller. I get Holmgren is out, but gotta play better. Chicago is 12-of-24 from 3. Let's see if OKC can salvage things in the second half. 2Q, 5:29 left: Bulls 55, Thunder 49Leonard Miller with a couple of layups and an outside jumper. Thunder call a timeout. They're in a 55-49 deficit against the Bulls with 5:29 left in the 2Q. Chicago is 11-of-19 from 3. Picked up right where they left off when they scored 53 points in the 4Q against the Sixers End 1Q: Bulls 32, Thunder 29This was supposed to be OKC's easiest opponent left on paper. The Bulls are showing you why the games are played on the courts. They're 8-of-14 from 3. The Thunder have been fine on offense despite Gilgeous-Alexander's slow start, but the defense needs to tighten up. 1Q, 7:00: Thunder 15, Bulls 14Wallace strips the ball away from Giddey on his spin move. Williams then goes all the way for the transition layup. Bulls call a timeout. Fast-paced start for both sides. Starting lineups:The Thunder will start Shai Gilgeous-Alexander, Cason Wallace, Lu Dort, Jalen Williams and Isaiah Hartenstein. The Bulls will start Josh Giddey, Tre Jones, Mata Buzelis, Isaac Okoro and Guerschon Yabusele.What channel is Bulls vs. Thunder game on today? Time, TV scheduleTV Channel: FanDuel Sports Network OklahomaStart time: 7 p.m. CTWhere to watch Bulls vs. Thunder on livestreamWatch Bulls vs. Thunder live on Fubo (free trial)Bulls vs. Thunder injury updatesThunder: Chet Holmgren (hip contusion) is out. Nikola Topic (G League assignment) is out. Brooks Barnhizer (G League two-way) is out. Thomas Sorber (torn ACL) is out.Bulls: Jaden Ivey (patellofemoral pain syndrome) is out. Noa Essengue (shoulder surgery) is out. Jalen Smith (calf strain) is out. Zach Collins (toe sprain) is out. Anfernee Simons (ulnar styloid fracture) is doubtful. Guerschon Yabusele (ankle sprain) is questionable. Nick Richards (elbow sprain) is questionable. Rob Dillingham (bilateral patella tendon tendonitis) is probable. Isaac Okoro (patellofemoral pain syndrome) is probable. Mac McClung (G League two-way) is out. Yuki Kawamura (G League two-way) is out.Thunder 2025-26 scheduleSunday, Mar. 29 vs. KnicksMonday, Mar. 30 vs. PistonsThursday, Apr. 2 vs. Lakers",
